# tests/remove-tool, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST of llm-step's inline `remove` tool: what the worker does with a
# queued batch of remove calls, including the refusals, and removing inside a
# source tree and a whole source tree. Like tests/chat-tools it mints the human
# turn itself and reads the turn commit back, because the subject is the worker,
# not `chat`.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/worker-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --bash:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --llm-step:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-step --stub:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-stub --tool:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test-tool --common:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test/worker-common.sh
